Title: "Labeled Expressions"
Id: "98edd056-5d9f-45f0-a8e8-16c63a2a7fcd"

Text: "A labeled expression attaches a label to an expression.

```mlg-fragment
(x + y)[:sum:]
(.x + y.)[:normalized:]
```

Only a grouped formulation may be labeled directly, and the wrapper may hold a declaration or specification as well as an expression:

```mlg-fragment
(.x is \real.)[:typed:]
(.*' := `*`.)[:operation:]
```

A label is discharged by a matching `[label]` entry in the enclosing item's `Justification:` section; an unmatched label is checked inline as usual.

Labels use the `[:...:]` token form and are distinct from structural label headers such as `[theorem.name]`. As lexer tokens they do not support stropped symbolic parts."
Id: "efe841b5-44ed-45f8-8d20-1aacb7fc9bdb"
